Chorik
[trigger none]
[vignette dungeons/signal_array]

# --- COLOR ---
# [] brass throat-button stamped with the Kesharat mark, worn smooth at the edges from constant touch
# [] tea cup chipped at the rim, held with both hands like a shield against the air
# [] his left boot sole cracked at the heel, leather split like old parchment
# [] fingers of his right hand tracing the seam of his tunic cuff, a habit when not working
# [] tea steam rising in thin wisps, curling above the cup but not spreading further
# [] one corner of his neck cloth folded unevenly, the crease not from pressing
# [] his hat tilted forward just enough to shadow his eyes, not for sun, for cover
# [] the teacup resting on a small patch of clean rock, the dust around it undisturbed
# [] the line of his jaw tight, not in anger, in the stillness of someone holding a breath
# [] a faint tremor in his left hand when he sets the cup down, barely visible
# --- end ---

FIXME(mundane): Chorik is next to you at the rest circle, teacup in both hands. The others have gone back to their own conversations across the rock but they are still in easy earshot.

choices:

* Try to draw him out = Speak low and see what he gives
    @if check negotiation correct:reason wrong:charm {
        FIXME(revelation): You speak low. You ask the kind of thing the others' patching has been keeping you from asking. He looks at his hands. He says he keeps thinking about leaving and never quite manages it. He says he has gaps in his memory. He says he thinks the mesa is driving him mad. He is more afraid than he is anything else, and afraid of being heard. Then Veran calls a question across the rock and Chorik straightens and answers it, and the moment closes.
        +add_tag signal_array.met_chorik
        +add_tag signal_array.chorik_unguarded
        +open "The Rest Interval"
    } @else {
        FIXME(dread): You speak low. He does not look at you. He sets his teacup down on the rock and stands up. He says something at normal volume to Veran about checking the cable runs, and crosses out of the rest circle to the half-built tower. The others watch him go without comment. You are alone on your side of the circle.
        +add_tag signal_array.met_chorik
        +open "The Rest Interval"
    }

* Let him be = Sit quietly without pressing
    FIXME(mundane): You let him sit. He does not seem grateful, exactly, but he relaxes a fraction. He finishes his tea. The conversation moves on around you without involving him.
    +add_tag signal_array.met_chorik
    +open "The Rest Interval"
